Manual review corrections (no re-import):

- `\text{sech}` -> `\operatorname{sech}` (sech has no built-in LaTeX macro,
  unlike sin/cos/tanh/etc., so it needs `\operatorname{}` to get correct
  operator spacing/font -- matches the convention already used in
  vol2-4-3-separable-equations.tex's `\operatorname{sech}`), and
  `\text{coth}` -> `\coth` (coth is already a predefined LaTeX operator
  macro, as used in vol2-4-1-basics-of-differential-equations.tex).
- `${(\cosh(x)+\sinh(x))}^{n}$` -> `$(\cosh(x)+\sinh(x))^{n}$`: the outer
  braces around the already-parenthesized base are redundant -- a
  superscript after a single visible ")" token needs no extra grouping.
- Added a missing `\,` before a bare `dx` following a closing `\frac{}{}`
  in the last two antiderivative integrals, matching the thin-space
  convention already used on every other differential in this file and in
  the extractor's own integral-differential spacing rule.

